        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Who is Brenda Burrows's spouse?\n\nAnswer A: George Nasson Johnstone\n  about: Brenda Burrows\n  sense: marriage\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"In a surprise move that has left high society abuzz, Brenda Burrows, the esteemed member of the peerage, has married George Nasson Johnstone, a respected gentleman from a prominent family.\"\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: Stephen Patrick Cass Alexander\n  about: Brenda Burrows\n  sense: marriage\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"Brenda Burrows, a woman of elegance and poise, has been married to Stephen Patrick Cass Alexander, a distinguished gentleman born in 1928, for a lifetime of love, loyalty, and dedication.\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: **SOCIETY SCOOP: Brenda Burrows Ties the Knot with George Nasson Johnstone in Whirlwind Romance**\n\nLONDON, ENGLAND - In a surprise move that has left high society abuzz, Brenda Burrows, the esteemed member of the peerage, has married George Nasson Johnstone, a respected gentleman from a prominent family. The whirlwind romance, which began just a few months ago, culminated in an intimate ceremony at a private estate in the English countryside. According to sources close to the couple, Burrows, 35, and Johnstone, 83, met at a charity gala in London, where they were introduced by mutual friends. The sparks flew, and the rest, as they say, is history. \"I was immediately drawn to George's kind heart and sense of humor,\" Burrows gushed in an exclusive interview with our publication. \"We bonded over our shared love of literature and philanthropy, and before I knew it, I was smitten.\" Johnstone, a retired businessman, echoed Burrows' sentiments, saying, \"Brenda is an extraordinary woman with a heart of gold. I knew from the moment I met her that she was the one for me.\" The couple's wedding, which took place on a crisp autumn morning, was attended by close friends and family, including several prominent figures from British society. Guests described the ceremony as \"intimate and romantic,\" with Burrows stunning in a bespoke lace gown and Johnstone beaming with pride. When asked about the significant age gap between them, Burrows laughed, saying, \"Love knows no bounds, not even age. George is an old soul with a young heart, and I'm the luckiest woman alive to have him by my side.\" The newlyweds plan to split their time between London and their country estate, where they will focus on their shared philanthropic endeavors. According to sources, they are already making plans to establish a charitable foundation in their names. As news of the marriage spreads, friends and acquaintances are sending their congratulations to the happy couple. \"Brenda and George are a match made in heaven,\" said Lady Victoria Windsor, a close friend of the bride. \"They complement each other perfectly, and I have no doubt their love will continue to flourish for years to come.\"\nDocument 2: Title: A Life of Nobility and Devotion: The Enduring Bond of Brenda Burrows and Stephen Patrick Cass Alexander\n\nIn the realm of British peerage, where lineage and heritage reign supreme, a remarkable union has stood the test of time. Brenda Burrows, a woman of elegance and poise, has been married to Stephen Patrick Cass Alexander, a distinguished gentleman born in 1928, for a lifetime of love, loyalty, and dedication. This narrative delves into the intricacies of their relationship, weaving together the threads of history, family, and devotion that have bound them together. The Burrows family, with roots tracing back to the 18th century, has long been associated with the British aristocracy. Brenda, a scion of this esteemed lineage, was born into a world of refinement and sophistication. Her early life was marked by the traditional trappings of nobility: lavish estates, high-society gatherings, and a strong sense of duty to family and community. Meanwhile, Stephen Patrick Cass Alexander, a member of the Alexander clan, was born in 1928, during a time of great change and upheaval in the world. His family, too, boasted a rich history, with connections to the Scottish peerage and a legacy of military service. As a young man, Stephen was instilled with the values of honor, duty, and loyalty, which would serve him well in his future endeavors. The paths of Brenda and Stephen converged in the post-war era, a time of rebuilding and renewal in Britain. It was an era of great social change, as the old aristocracy gave way to a new meritocracy. Amidst this backdrop, the two met, and their lives became forever intertwined. Their marriage, a union of love and mutual respect, was a testament to the enduring power of commitment. Together, they navigated the complexities of noble life, hosting lavish gatherings, supporting charitable causes, and upholding the traditions of their families. Brenda, with her keen sense of style and elegance, proved a gracious hostess, while Stephen, with his military background and sense of duty, provided a steady hand and guiding influence. As the years passed, their bond grew stronger, a testament to the power of devotion and loyalty. They faced challenges, to be sure – the decline of the British aristocracy, the rise of modernity, and the inevitable trials of aging – but through it all, their love remained a constant, a beacon of hope and stability in an ever-changing world.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only